1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
Thick yellow-green mucus and a nose that won't clear?

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:10,319
That's sinusitis - swollen, blocked sinus openings trap fluid inside and fuel the inflammation.

3
00:00:10,639 --> 00:00:13,279
Three everyday habits make that blockage worse.

4
00:00:13,599 --> 00:00:15,939
First, blowing your nose too hard.

5
00:00:16,259 --> 00:00:23,937
A hard blow creates about ten times more pressure than a cough, and that pressure pushes mucus straight into your sinus cavities.

6
00:00:24,257 --> 00:00:28,257
Second, using decongestant spray for more than three days.

7
00:00:28,577 --> 00:00:39,735
It shrinks blood vessels fast, but push past that limit and your nasal lining rebounds, swelling worse than before - doctors call it rhinitis medicamentosa.

8
00:00:40,055 --> 00:00:43,874
Finally, spending hours in dry indoor air.

9
00:00:44,194 --> 00:00:50,733
Low humidity thickens mucus and slows the cilia that sweep it out, so drainage backs up.

10
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:53,653
Blow one nostril at a time, gently.

11
00:00:53,973 --> 00:00:56,873
Cap decongestant spray at three days.

12
00:00:57,193 --> 00:01:03,292
Keep indoor humidity near 40 to 50 percent, and drink plenty of water to thin the mucus.

13
00:01:03,612 --> 00:01:07,771
If yellow-green congestion drags on past ten days, see a doctor.
